React Manual

Apple users installation 
1.Install homebrew. In the command line, type following:

/bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"

echo 'eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"' >> ~/.zprofile

eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"

2.. In the command line, type following to install mysql:

brew install node


3. Go to /SBU_25F_CSE416/frontend and install packages using "npm install"


2. run by typing "npm run dev"

Window users installation
1. Go to https://nodejs.org/en and click Node.js. Download window installer. 

2, Go to ..\SBU_25F_CSE416\frontend and install packages using "npm install"

3, run by typing "npm run dev"


Java Spring Boot Manual

1. To initialize, you need to update your Java version to 25. 
- Please check and download the correct version for your system https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/downloads/ and set the java path in your environment. 

3. . Install Maven.
- Download the latest Maven version from: https://maven.apache.org/download.cgi
- Extract and set the MAVEN_HOME path in your environment variables.
- Add Maven to your PATH.
- For apple users, you can type this in the command line : brew install maven

2.Install visual studio code. https://code.visualstudio.com/Download based  on your system. 

3,In VScode extensions, install "Extension Pack for Java" and "Spring Boot Extension Pack"

3. Go to ..\SBU_25F_CSE416\backend\src\main\java\edu\sbu\cse416\sam_system\SamSystemApplication.java and press control + shift + p

4. Click "Java: Clean Java Language Server Workspace"

To Run Spring boot,  
5. Go to ..\SBU_25F_CSE416\backend\src\main\java\edu\sbu\cse416\sam_system\SamSystemApplication.java. Press "Run Java" button, which is located in upper right side

MySQL Database Manual

Apple users installation 
1.Install homebrew. In the command line, type following:

/bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"

echo 'eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"' >> ~/.zprofile
eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"

2,Now we installed homebrew. In the command line, type following to install mysql:

brew update
brew install mysql

To run MySQL service, 
type the following in the command line :

brew services start mysql

mysql -u root


Windows users installation
1. Download the MySQL Installer from https://dev.mysql.com/downloads/installer/.


2 .Choose MySQL Server and optionally Workbench


3. Choose “Server Only” or “Full” setup


4. Set up root password

5. Configure port : 3306 (default port)

5. After installation, type mysql -u root -p 
and type your password for checking information in the database

Note: Some constants are hardcoded in the project:

Database credentials: ../backend/src/main/resources/application.properties
   - spring.datasource.username=root
   - spring.datasource.password=YOUR_PASSWORD
   Please update these values according to your local database setup.

